# Local environment
.env
.env.local

# Go
/bin/
*.test
*.out
# Binaries left by `go build ./...`, which writes one per main package beside the module.
#
# A name per command, and the list went stale once already: it named the four API binaries
# that merged into `api`, so the first `go build ./...` after the merge committed three
# hundred-megabyte executables and GitHub refused the push. Adding a command means adding
# it here, which is the cost of not ignoring a whole directory that also holds go.mod.
/apps/backend/api
/apps/backend/analytics-writer
/apps/backend/archive-writer
/apps/backend/archivecheck
/apps/backend/billing-writer
/apps/backend/cohortcheck
/apps/backend/migrate
/apps/backend/wiresize
/apps/backend/worker

# Rust. Anchored like the Go binaries above, so a `target/` appearing anywhere else is a
# deliberate decision rather than a silent one. Cargo.lock IS committed: this workspace
# produces a shippable artifact (a cdylib/staticlib inside somebody's game), not a library
# crate, so a reproducible build matters.
/sdk/target/

# Unity. The generated project files and caches only — `.meta` files must stay tracked, or
# a package manager install produces a package Unity cannot resolve.
/sdk/unity/Library/
/sdk/unity/Temp/
/sdk/unity/Obj/
/sdk/unity/Logs/
/sdk/unity/*.csproj
/sdk/unity/*.sln

# The native libraries the package links against are a release artifact, not a source file:
# `./install-plugins.sh` puts them here from sdk/target. One unstripped iOS archive is 21 MB
# against ~550 KB of linked code, and eight platforms of that would be most of the repository.
#
# By extension rather than by folder, because the `.meta` files beside them MUST stay tracked:
# they carry the per-platform importer settings, and a wrong one is a DllNotFoundException in
# somebody's build and nothing in the Editor.
/sdk/unity/Runtime/Plugins/**/*.a
/sdk/unity/Runtime/Plugins/**/*.so
/sdk/unity/Runtime/Plugins/**/*.dylib
/sdk/unity/Runtime/Plugins/**/*.dll

# Node
node_modules/
.nuxt/
.output/
dist/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Local data volumes
infra/**/data/

# Ent generates into apps/backend/ent; the schema is the source, but the
# generated client is committed so a clone builds without a codegen step.
.data/
